{"slug":"types","number":"8","title":"Types, materials and assets","file":"spec/core/08-types.md","sections":[{"id":"8.1","number":"8.1","title":"Types"},{"id":"8.2","number":"8.2","title":"Resolving typed properties"},{"id":"8.3","number":"8.3","title":"Wall types and layers"},{"id":"8.4","number":"8.4","title":"Door and window types"},{"id":"8.5","number":"8.5","title":"Materials"},{"id":"8.6","number":"8.6","title":"Assets"},{"id":"8.7","number":"8.7","title":"Lints"}],"blocks":[{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"8.1","number":"8.1","c":["Types"]},{"t":"p","c":["A ",{"t":"strong","c":["type"]}," is a reusable definition — a wall assembly, a door, a window — that elements refer to instead of repeating (FLR-ADR-003). Change the type, and every element that uses it changes."]},{"t":"p","c":["Types live in the ",{"t":"code","v":"types"}," collection, and each has a ",{"t":"code","v":"kind"},":"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null],"head":[[{"t":"code","v":"kind"}],["Used by"],["Its members"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"\"wallType\""}],[{"t":"code","v":"Wall.type"}],[{"t":"a","href":"#8.3","c":["8.3"]}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"\"doorType\""}],[{"t":"code","v":"Opening.fill"}],[{"t":"a","href":"#8.4","c":["8.4"]}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"\"windowType\""}],[{"t":"code","v":"Opening.fill"}],[{"t":"a","href":"#8.4","c":["8.4"]}]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.1.1","level":"MUST","c":["A type MUST have a ",{"t":"code","v":"kind"}," from this table."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.1.2","level":"MAY","c":["Every type MAY also carry ",{"t":"code","v":"name"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensions"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"extras"}," (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/model#1.4","c":["1.4"]},")."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["Common types — a 2×4 interior partition, a 2×6 exterior wall, a 36-inch door — are published as a non-normative starter library. A document embeds every type it uses; it never refers to a library by URL, so it is always complete on its own."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"8.2","number":"8.2","c":["Resolving typed properties"]},{"t":"p","c":["Some members of an element are ",{"t":"strong","c":["typed properties"]},": the element may set them itself, or inherit them from its type. In core 0.1 they are a wall's ",{"t":"code","v":"layers"}," (from its ",{"t":"code","v":"type"},") and an opening's ",{"t":"code","v":"width"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"height"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"sill"}," (from its ",{"t":"code","v":"fill"},")."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.2.1","level":"MUST","c":["A reader MUST resolve a typed property to the element's own member if present, otherwise to its type's member if present, otherwise to the property's default if it has one."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["An element's own value always wins over its type's — the rule IFC calls an occurrence overriding its type. A typed property has no constant default at the element (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/model#1.5","c":["1.5"]},"): an opening that states ",{"t":"code","v":"\"sill\": 0"}," overrides a window type's sill, so a writer never omits it."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"8.3","number":"8.3","c":["Wall types and layers"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Default"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"kind"}],[{"t":"code","v":"\"wallType\""}],["—"],[{"t":"a","href":"#8.1","c":["8.1"]}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"layers"}],["array of at least one layer"],["— (always present)"],["the assembly, from the wall's left (exterior) face to its right (interior) face"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"name"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensions"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extras"}],[],[],[{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/model#1.4","c":["1.4"]}]]]},{"t":"p","c":["A ",{"t":"strong","c":["layer"]},":"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Default"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"thickness"}],["length"],["— (always present)"],["the layer's thickness"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"function"}],["layer function (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/taxonomy#4.3","c":["4.3"]},")"],["— (always present)"],["what the layer does"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"material"}],["reference to a material"],["absent"],["what it is made of"]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.3.1","level":"MUST","c":["A ",{"t":"code","v":"layers"}," array MUST contain at least one layer, and every layer's ",{"t":"code","v":"thickness"}," MUST be greater than zero."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["A wall's own ",{"t":"code","v":"layers"}," member, when present, follows the same rules and replaces its type's layers entirely."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"8.4","number":"8.4","c":["Door and window types"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Default"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"kind"}],[{"t":"code","v":"\"doorType\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"windowType\""}],["—"],[{"t":"a","href":"#8.1","c":["8.1"]}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"width"}],["length"],["absent"],["the width of every opening it fills, unless the opening overrides it"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"height"}],["length"],["absent"],["likewise, the height"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"sill"}],["length"],["absent"],["likewise, the sill"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"name"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensions"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extras"}],[],[],[{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/model#1.4","c":["1.4"]}]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.4.1","level":"MUST","c":["A door or window type's ",{"t":"code","v":"width"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"height"},", when present, MUST be greater than zero, and its ",{"t":"code","v":"sill"}," MUST NOT be negative."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["Operation, frame, glazing and hardware are defined in a later draft."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"8.5","number":"8.5","c":["Materials"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Default"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"color"}],[{"t":"code","v":"\"#rrggbb\""},", lowercase hexadecimal sRGB"],["absent"],["the material's base colour"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"texture"}],[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"asset\": reference to an asset, \"size\": [w, h] }"},", both always present"],["absent"],["an image tiled across the surface; one tile covers ",{"t":"code","v":"w"}," by ",{"t":"code","v":"h"}," base units"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"name"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensions"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extras"}],[],[],[{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/model#1.4","c":["1.4"]}]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.5.1","level":"MUST","c":["A material's ",{"t":"code","v":"color"}," MUST match ",{"t":"code","v":"^#[0-9a-f]{6}$"},"."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.5.2","level":"MUST","c":["A texture's ",{"t":"code","v":"size"}," MUST be two lengths greater than zero."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["Physically based rendering properties are defined in a later draft. A texture's real-world size is what makes a dropped-in photo of a tile the right scale on every wall."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"8.6","number":"8.6","c":["Assets"]},{"t":"p","c":["An ",{"t":"strong","c":["asset"]}," is a file a document refers to — a texture image now; a glTF model or a 2D symbol in later drafts and extensions."]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Default"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"path"}],["relative path"],["absent"],["where the file is, relative to the document (packaged with it)"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"uri"}],["an absolute URI (RFC 3986) whose scheme is ",{"t":"code","v":"https"}," and which has an authority"],["absent"],["where the file is on the web"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"sha256"}],["64 lowercase hexadecimal digits"],["— (always present)"],["the SHA-256 digest of the file's bytes"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"mediaType"}],["a media type ",{"t":"code","v":"type/subtype"}," as RFC 6838 §4.2 defines it, without parameters, such as ",{"t":"code","v":"\"image/png\""}],["— (always present)"],["what kind of file it is"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"name"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensions"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extras"}],[],[],[{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/model#1.4","c":["1.4"]}]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.6.1","level":"MUST","c":["An asset MUST have exactly one of ",{"t":"code","v":"path"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"uri"},"."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.6.2","level":"MUST","c":["A ",{"t":"code","v":"path"}," MUST be relative, use ",{"t":"code","v":"/"}," as its separator, contain no empty, ",{"t":"code","v":"."}," or ",{"t":"code","v":".."}," segment, and have no ",{"t":"code","v":":"}," in its first segment."]}," A path is a path, not a URI reference: it is not percent-encoded."]},{"t":"p","c":["The digest makes an asset verifiable wherever it is found, and lets a store keep one copy of a texture used by many projects. An asset by ",{"t":"code","v":"uri"}," makes the document depend on someone else's server; validators report it as a lint (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-007"},")."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"8.7","number":"8.7","c":["Lints"]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-8.7.1","level":"SHOULD","c":["A validator SHOULD report these with the codes of ",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/diagnostics","c":["chapter 10"]},"."]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Unused type, material or asset"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-006"},", information): nothing refers to it."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["External asset"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-007"},", warning): an asset located by ",{"t":"code","v":"uri"},"."]}]]}]}
